]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Shared in-process family-successor engine[/bold #D7AFFF]                     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]successor[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]successor: extract the runner's repeated become-the-next-family-member [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]dance into one engine and migrate the plan-approval coder hand-off and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the questions follow-up onto it, behavior unchanged.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Shared pending-handoff marker protocol[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]handoff[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]handoff: give the four marker-writing CLI hand-offs one guard/write/kill[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]helper and one marker registry, and register the pipe marker there.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Shared out-of-process family spawn[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]spawn[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]spawn: put the detached child spawn and the family-attach env encoding [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]behind one primitive that monitor follow-up and retry spawn both call.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The `sase pipe` command[/bold #D7AFFF]                                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]pipe[dim] · [dim][/dim]after successor, handoff[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]pipe: add the CLI, its guards and chain bound, the pending marker it [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]writes, and the runner adoption that continues as the piped successor.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The `/sase_pipe` skill and user documentation[/bold #D7AFFF]